messages:
Alex: Quick heads-up — saw duplicated NVTX range ids in perfetto across concurrent requests. Ranges from KV_prefetch and kernel_choice are getting aggregated and it's hiding hotspots.
Maria: ack, can you drop a link to the trace?
Alex: perfetto: https://perfetto.app/trace/abcd1234 — check timeline ~00:04:12. Two different requests have ranges named \"kv_prefetch\" with the same id and they merge in the UI.
Sam: that's usually because we're reusing a small id space or a counter that overlaps per thread. Are we assigning explicit nvtx ids anywhere?
Alex: We were using a per-thread incremental counter (reset on thread startup). Under high concurrency counters collide. nsys also shows nvtx range id 6421 present on multiple tids.
Jia: Proposed naming pattern: \"<span-type>/<short-request-hash>/<phase>\" e.g. \"kvcache/pre1234b/prefetch\" — readable, groups by type but unique per request. Keep < 64 chars.
Maria: I like the request-hash suffix. Also: for kernel selection spans maybe include kernel family only (eg \"gemm32x32\") not full param dump. We can attach attributes for params.
Sam: Also strongly +1 to suppress per-token NVTX ranges. They explode trace size. Emit per-request spans and one kernel timeline per batch instead.
Alex: Agreed. For nvtx id generation let's switch to a stable 32-bit hash of (request_id + span_name) to avoid collisions across threads. Example code snippet below.

Alex: ```
// simple FNV-1a 32-bit of (request_id + ":" + span_name)
uint32_t fnv1a32(const std::string &s) {
  uint32_t h = 0x811c9dc5;
  for (char c : s) h = (h ^ (uint8_t)c) * 0x01000193;
  return h;
}
uint32_t nvtx_id = fnv1a32(request_id + ":" + span_name);
nvtxRangePushExA(..., nvtx_id, name);
```

Sam: Add a fallback when request_id is missing: use thread_id + monotonic counter and emit a short log if duplicates detected in CI traces.
Jia: We should also standardize short attribute tags to keep UI compact, e.g. tags: \"r:pre\" (request prefetch), \"k:sel\" (kernel select), \"q:bat\" (batch size). Perfetto will show them in the span details.
Alex: I'll open a PR that does: 1) rename spans to include short request-hash, 2) switch id generator to fnv1a32 hash, 3) suppress per-token NVTX, 4) emit only batch-level kernel spans and attach attributes, 5) upload perfetto artifact in CI. Assigning review to @Sam.
trace-bot: perf run uploaded: s3://redwood-perf/1745519000/nvtx-traces/perfetto.pbz :thumbsup:
Sam: On it. I'll patch the kernel-selection emitter to use batch-level range and only include kernel name when it changes within the batch. Also will add duplicate-detection alert log to staging CI.
Maria: thanks — I'll schedule nsys runs on staging with the new naming and run the perfetto diff to confirm merges are gone.
Alex: thanks all :rocket:
